---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Works" currentPath="/works">
  <span class="meta">III · Works</span>
  <h1>Resolved structures</h1>

  <div class="page-content">
    <p class="lead">
      A Work begins with an intention, not a style. Its hierarchy, pacing,
      navigation and expression are resolved around what the visitor needs to do.
    </p>

    <article class="work" id="atlas">
      <div class="work-meta">
        <span>W01 · Version 1.0</span>
        <span>Recovered edition · 2026</span>
      </div>
      <h2>Atlas</h2>
      <p class="abstract">A photographer website system composed of three architectures, each built for a different relationship between work and viewer.</p>

      <ol class="volume-list">
        <li><span>I</span><strong>Still</strong><p>Singular images, given undivided attention.</p></li>
        <li><span>II</span><strong>Sequence</strong><p>Bodies of work whose meaning develops through order.</p></li>
        <li><span>III</span><strong>Index</strong><p>Range and relevance made legible for professional evaluation.</p></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="work-entry">
        <p class="availability">Works 01 · Live demonstration</p>
        <a class="work-entry__link" href="/works/atlas/" style="text-decoration: none;">Enter <span aria-hidden="true" style="font-size: .55em; line-height: 1;">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="work" id="aurele">
      <div class="work-meta">
        <span>W02 · Version 1.0</span>
        <span>Public record edition · 2026</span>
      </div>
      <h2>Aurèle</h2>
      <p class="abstract">An editorial publishing structure whose identity remains constant while the record changes pace.</p>

      <ol class="volume-list">
        <li><span>I</span><strong>Dispatch</strong><p>What is known now, reported precisely and left open to revision.</p></li>
        <li><span>II</span><strong>Chronicle</strong><p>What becomes known over time, with sequence and correction preserved.</p></li>
        <li><span>III</span><strong>Review</strong><p>What the completed record has come to mean.</p></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="work-entry">
        <p class="availability">Works 02 · Complete demonstration</p>
        <a class="work-entry__link" href="/works/aurele/" style="text-decoration: none;">Enter <span aria-hidden="true" style="font-size: .55em; line-height: 1;">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="work" id="allure">
      <div class="work-meta">
        <span>W03 · In development</span>
        <span>Demonstration record · 2026</span>
      </div>
      <h2>Allure</h2>
      <p class="abstract">A portfolio structure that presents one professional record through three resolved hierarchies.</p>

      <ol class="volume-list">
        <li><span>I</span><strong>Retenue</strong><p>Work organised by fact and proof.</p></li>
        <li><span>II</span><strong>Éclat</strong><p>Work organised by capability and connection.</p></li>
        <li><span>III</span><strong>Poise</strong><p>Work organised by time and consequence.</p></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="work-entry">
        <p class="availability">Works 03 · Working demonstration</p>
        <a class="work-entry__link" href="/works/allure/" style="text-decoration: none;">Enter <span aria-hidden="true" style="font-size: .55em; line-height: 1;">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-content { max-width: 760px; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.85; font-style: italic; }
  .work { margin-top: 4rem; padding-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-ink); }
  .work + .work { margin-top: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 8rem); }
  .work-meta { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 2rem; font-family: var(--font-ui); font-size: var(--text-micro); letter-spacing: var(--tracking-widest); text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-secondary); }
  :global(.main--content) .work h2 { font-family: var(--font-display) !important; font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.5rem) !important; font-weight: var(--weight-light) !important; line-height: 1 !important; letter-spacing: 0 !important; text-transform: none !important; color: var(--color-ink) !important; margin: 3rem 0 1.5rem !important; }
  .abstract { font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--color-secondary); }
  .volume-list { list-style: none; margin: 3rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .volume-list li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 40px 110px 1fr; gap: 1rem; align-items: baseline; padding: 1.25rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .volume-list span { font-family: var(--font-ui); font-size: var(--text-micro); color: var(--color-secondary); }
  .volume-list strong { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: var(--weight-regular); }
  .volume-list p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-secondary); }
  :global(.main--content) .availability { font-family: var(--font-ui) !important; font-size: var(--text-micro) !important; font-style: normal !important; letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide) !important; line-height: 1.5 !important; text-transform: uppercase !important; color: var(--color-secondary) !important; }
  .work-entry { display: grid; justify-items: start; gap: .75rem; }
  .work-entry__link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .55rem; padding: 0; border: 0; font-family: var(--font-ui); font-size: var(--text-micro); font-weight: var(--weight-medium); letter-spacing: var(--tracking-widest); text-decoration: none !important; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-ink); }
  .work-entry__link span { font-size: .55em; line-height: 1; }
  .work-entry__link:hover { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .work-entry .availability { margin: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .volume-list li { grid-template-columns: 28px 1fr; } .volume-list p { grid-column: 2; } }
</style>
